# Playwright constitution

Hard constraints for every task. Details live in `playwright-conventions.mdc` and skills.

## Agent governance

Behavioral contract (not hook-enforced). Audit first; edit second.

### Audit-then-edit

Before any non-trivial edit: explore the relevant files, conventions, and skills. Do not invent a path, enum, env var, credential, or user-facing message — ask or explore until verified.

### Proposal (before editing)

Every non-trivial task emits a **Proposal** block first:

| Field | Content |
|---|---|
| Scope | What will change (files / behavior) |
| Confidence | Integer 1–10 |
| Rationale | Why this approach |
| Unknowns | Gaps, assumptions, missing inputs |

### Confidence gate

| Score | Action |
|---|---|
| **< 5** | Do not proceed — ask for the missing input |
| **5–7** | Proceed only with unknowns listed and human approval |
| **≥ 8** | Proceed |

## MUST

| Rule | Meaning |
|---|---|
| Role-based locators | `getByRole` / label first; `getByTestId` only with a why-comment; never CSS/XPath |
| Web-first assertions | `expect(locator)…` only; no `waitForTimeout`, no `isVisible()` snapshots |
| `storageState` auth | Feature tests use setup project auth; UI login only for login-page tests |
| Unique self-cleaning data | Faker/unique names; every create cleans up in `finally` / fixture |
| One tag per test | Exactly one of `@smoke` · `@sanity` · `@regression` · `@api` · `@e2e` · `@destructive` on each `test(…)` — never on `describe` |
| State revert hooks | Any test that mutates shared/global state MUST revert in `afterEach` / `afterAll` |

## SHOULD

| Rule | Meaning |
|---|---|
| Faker factories | Build test data via factories, not ad-hoc inline strings |
| Enums for repeated strings | Shared labels, statuses, routes → typed constants/enums |
| JSDoc on action methods | Document POM actions (params, side effects, return) |

## WON'T

| Rule | Meaning |
|---|---|
| XPath | Never |
| `waitForTimeout` | Never — use web-first waits |
| Hardcoded secrets | Env / `storageState` only |
| `any` | Never in specs, POMs, or helpers |
| Weakened assertions | Never heal by loosening expected behavior |
| Healing a real bug | Heal locator drift only; file bugs for app defects |
| Tags on `describe` | Tags belong on individual tests only |
| Ad-hoc / multiple tags | Only the six allowed tags; exactly one per test |

